  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FCDO Support to Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The&#x202f;project&#x202f;will pilot a&#x202f;mental&#x202f;health and&#x202f;psychosocial&#x202f;support (MHPSS)&#x202f;service&#x202f;delivery model&#x202f;for&#x202f;both displaced Ukrainian and vulnerable Moldovan communities, with a specific focus on older people (60+) and&#x202f;people&#x202f;with disabilities.&#x202f;The intervention aims to strengthen&#x202f;last-mile social protection delivery&#x202f;capacity by pairing Moldovan Red Cross Society (MRCS) volunteers with&#x202f;public-sector&#x202f;social assistance specialist staff. Together, they will deliver safe, inclusive and accessible psychosocial support within both Refugee Accommodation Centres&#x202f;(RACs) and a MRCS Community&#x202f;Centre. Capacity&#x2011;building activities for personnel delivering the programme will be planned and implemented jointly by MRCS, IFRC and BRC throughout the project period, ensuring appropriate skills and knowledge to work effectively with and deliver support to the targeted vulnerable populations. This is a tripartite partnership between BRC, IFRC, and MRCS, with BRC acting as the grant holder and direct subcontracting arrangements in place with both MRCS and IFRC.</narrative>
  </description>
